spec: specs/di.md stage 3 (the gap di-dogfood found)

why: `Needs.of[Root]` treats every unresolved input as something the
  PLACE provides, and a real root's inputs are mixed — a database is
  the place's, a Timer is the process's own. Today the only answers
  are a lie (`given Needs[Timer] = Needs(Need.…)`) or losing the
  guarantee.

what: `Needs` becomes a two-case declaration — Place(need) and
  Runtime() — with `Needs(need)` unchanged for the place and
  `Needs.runtime` for the rest; `Needs.of` collects the places and
  still fails to compile on an input that declares neither. Timer and
  Scheduler declared runtime in the companion, where implicit scope
  finds them for any application.

next: implement, test a mixed root, keep the missing-declaration error
